2.0 Competition Details
2.1 Resources 
Competitors will be given a presentation station where they can display their projects - any physical and virtual prototypes - such that judges and other attendees can walk around it. Hence an exhibition hall will be provided  to allow competitors to set up displays and perform
presentations to the judges. This hall will be in a central location and will be open to
the public during the competition.


The following equipment will be made available to all competitors during the competition
time period:
* A table to display presentations
* Electrical power supply for each team
* Internet source
Teams opting to build a physical prototype must secure their own funding and materials; no financial support or physical resources will be provided by the competition. 
2.2 Competition Personnel
The Competition Lead: Responsible for the implementation of the competition. The Competition Lead must be present at all of the presentations and be available to competitors and judges at any time for questions and requests.


Competition Director(s): Responsible for supporting the Competition Lead during the implementation of the competition. The Directors must be available to competitors and judges for questions and requests.


Official Timekeeper: Responsible for enforcing time limits during the presentations.


Judges: A minimum of three (3) judges are required to assess the project design, feasibility, innovation, and communication skills of the competitors. Judges in this category will come from a variety of backgrounds including communications, sales and technical or consulting engineering.
