2.3 Competitor Deliverables
Deliverables should be uploaded to this form before the deadline mentioned in Section 3.0. Teams having technical difficulty are permitted to send their files to yec@lasengsoc.com 
The subject line of their email should be the file name format mentioned below.


Design Summary: Prior to the competition, the team must submit a Design Summary. 
* The purpose of this document is for the judges and organizers to be prepared ahead of time for the topics. This Summary will follow conventional formatting characteristics (12 point Arial or Times New Roman font, 1.15 line spacing, 1” paper margins) and is limited to 1 page. The design summary must include, but is not limited to:
* Team name
* Team members
* Design topic and description
* Longevity Justification (How the design ensures durability and low maintenance)
* Citations in IEEE format
The file name should be [TeamName] - Design Summary Submission - YEC Innovative Design. Note: The Design Summary text must fit on 1 page. However, the IEEE reference list may be placed on an uncounted 2nd page if additional space is needed.


Presentation Slides: Competitors must compose a visual to present to the judges.
* The slides will be used to aid the judges in keeping notes and providing feedback when necessary and desired.
* The slides do not need to be submitted until just before beginning the presentation. 


The file name should be [TeamName] - Slidedeck Submission - YEC Innovative Design
2.3.1 Technical Details
Time Keeping: Points will be deducted if competitors do not adhere to the time limit. The following rules will be adhered to with respect to timekeeping: 
* Time is not halted when a judge asks a question during the presentation. 
* Presenters will be asked to stop their presentation if they exceed 5 minutes. Time to both ask and answer questions during the questioning period will be counted. 






