4.0 Challenge
Identify a significant, recurring issue within any domain—such as infrastructure, healthcare, environmental conservation, or public services—and develop an engineering solution that prioritizes durability and minimal upkeep. Competitors are encouraged to explore innovative approaches that ensure their solution remains relevant, cost-effective, and impactful over time, fostering a stable and sustainable future with minimal need for rework. Solutions should take into account social, economic, and environmental (SEE) factors while adhering to ethical engineering standards. Teams may propose either a physical model or a digital system solution, ensuring that it is accessible, inclusive, and scalable.
4.1 Examples  


Participants may choose to focus on one of the following areas (but are not limited to):
* Healthcare System Accessibility
* Pandemic Preparedness
* Environmental Disaster Response (e.g., hurricanes, earthquakes)
* Infrastructure for a Growing Population
* Affordable Housing Solutions
* Economic Resilience Amidst Inflation
* Climate Change Mitigation
* Sustainable Energy Solutions
* Cybersecurity and Crime Prevention
